/* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The range, as data. `window.DEVICES`.

   ── Why this is a package and no longer a variable in one tool ──
   It was declared inline in `Stick-Maker/public/index.html`, which was correct
   while one tool read it. Two do now — the Stick Maker prints a type plate from
   it and the Passport builder builds a page from it — and a catalogue copied
   into a second file is a catalogue that disagrees with itself the first time a
   specification is corrected in one of them. Same argument the UI kit makes, and
   the same mechanism carries it: source here, copies written into each project's
   `public/assets/devices/` by `ui-kit/sync.mjs`.

   ── What a record holds ──
     id       the tool's own key
     code     the matrix code — the join to `range.js`, which is where the range is
              typed. Every record has one as of 2026-09-11; a record without one is a
              drawing of a product that does not exist, and build-csv says so
     label    what a person calls it
     group    the series it belongs to, which is how the pickers are grouped
     kind     the product matrix's Name column — what the thing *is*
     colours  the finishes it exists in
     imgs     the photograph per finish, keyed by finish; `null` = one picture
     w, h     the lockup's drawn size
     svg      the lockup itself, `currentColor`, drawn by the design library
     code, word, batch, fill, compat, fn, comp — the loading fields, on sacks only

   Seeded from `docs/PRODUCT-MATRIX.md`. Where the matrix is silent this file is silent
   too: `kind` is empty on A2 and SMARTANK because the matrix has no row for them,
   and an empty kind drops a line where a plausible one would be a claim about a
   product printed on the document that certifies it.

   ⚠ No GTINs here. Three sources disagree about who owns reference `00`, and the
   answer is in myGS1 → GTIN-Manager and nowhere else (`docs/PRODUCT-MATRIX.md` §5,
   `Digital-Passport-Landing-Page/README.md`). A number written here would be read by both tools as
   settled, printed onto a carton, and wrong.
   ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
